{"text": "Association ANCA\n\nTenet err Hagare epraon Peters on 8\n\nALASKA FEDERATION\nOFMATIVES\n\nJuly 15, 2019\n\nSen. Lora Reinbold\n\u2018Alaska State Legislature\nState Capitol, Rm. 427\nJuneau, AK 99801\n\u2018Senator Lora Reinbold@akleg gov\n\nDear Senator Reinbold,\n\n\u2018The Alaska Federation of Natives (AFN), ANCSA Regional Association (ARA), and\n\u2018Alaska Native Village Corporation Association (ANVCA) are statewide Native\n\u2018organizations with questions and concerns about your July 11 Facebook post.' While\nwe have not had the pleasure of an introduction, we hope to make your acquaintance\n's00n to clear up some of the factual errors contained in your post.\n\nAEN Is the oldest and largest statewide Native organization in Alaska. Our membership\nincludes all 12 regional for-profit corporations, all 12 regional non-profit organizations,\n172 village for-profit corporations, and 191 of Alaska's federally recognized tribes. Our\nmission, among other things, is to advance and enhance the political voice of the Alaska\nNative community on matters of critical importance. in total, AFN represents one in five\nAlaskans through our membership.\n\nARA represents the presidents and chief executive officers of the 12 Alaska Native\nRegional Corporations created pursuant to the Alaska Native Claims Settlement Act of\n1971 (ANCSA). Our association exists to promote and foster the economic strength of\nthe Native regional corporations on behalf of our collective 130,000 shareholders. Our\nmission is to create a sustainable socioeconomic future for Alaska Native peoples.\nANVCA represents 177 village and urban corporations established under the Alaska\nNative Claims Settlement Act of 1971. Our mission is to promote the success of Native\nvillage corporations, while protecting Native lands. Like AFN, ANVCA represents\nupwards of 150,000 Alaskan through our members.\n\n\u2018As noted above, we have questions about your Facebook post.\n\n* Soe attached screenshot from Senator Lora Reinbold\u2019s Facebook page.",
